1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:04,677
This is the Halara Coffee Club Point of Sale and Inventory System:

2
00:00:04,677 --> 00:00:09,225
an Android tablet app for the staff, and a web dashboard for the admin.

3
00:00:10,825 --> 00:00:13,950
Part one: the staff app on the Android tablet.

4
00:00:15,550 --> 00:00:17,902
Staff sign in with their own account.

5
00:00:17,902 --> 00:00:20,000
Here we use the demo credentials.

6
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:25,575
The home screen shows today's sales, transactions, and low-stock alerts.

7
00:00:26,575 --> 00:00:29,888
Before taking orders, the cashier must open a shift,

8
00:00:29,888 --> 00:00:31,800
so every payment is traceable.

9
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:37,925
The cashier enters the starting cash, one thousand pesos, and opens the shift.

10
00:00:38,925 --> 00:00:40,813
Each menu item shows its price,

11
00:00:40,813 --> 00:00:45,075
and how many servings can still be made from the ingredients in stock.

12
00:00:46,075 --> 00:00:49,801
When an ingredient runs out, like the ham for this sandwich,

13
00:00:49,801 --> 00:00:51,975
the item is disabled automatically.

14
00:00:52,975 --> 00:00:57,250
Staff filter by category, and tap plus to add items to the order.

15
00:01:00,025 --> 00:01:02,675
In the cart, quantities can be adjusted.

16
00:01:03,675 --> 00:01:06,088
Cash, G-Cash, and Maya are supported.

17
00:01:06,088 --> 00:01:10,000
For cash, quick-amount buttons compute the change instantly.

18
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:13,150
Once confirmed, the sale is saved,

19
00:01:13,150 --> 00:01:16,121
recipe ingredients are deducted from inventory,

20
00:01:16,121 --> 00:01:19,725
and the receipt prints directly to the Bluetooth printer.

21
00:01:20,725 --> 00:01:24,133
For G-Cash or Maya, the store's QR code is shown.

22
00:01:24,133 --> 00:01:27,750
The cashier confirms only after the payment arrives.

23
00:01:35,125 --> 00:01:39,862
The Orders screen lists every transaction, where receipts can be reprinted,

24
00:01:39,862 --> 00:01:41,125
and orders refunded.

25
00:01:42,125 --> 00:01:47,000
Staff can also check raw material stock, with low and out-of-stock labels.

26
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:52,386
At the end of the shift, the cashier counts the drawer and closes the shift.

27
00:01:52,386 --> 00:01:55,675
The system records any difference from the expected cash.

28
00:01:56,675 --> 00:01:59,575
Part two: the admin dashboard on the web.

29
00:02:01,175 --> 00:02:03,582
On the web, users choose their role.

30
00:02:03,582 --> 00:02:06,525
Only admin accounts can open the admin side.

31
00:02:07,525 --> 00:02:12,312
The dashboard summarizes sales, transactions, stock alerts, and products.

32
00:02:12,312 --> 00:02:16,575
The tablet orders we just made already appear here, in real time.

33
00:02:17,575 --> 00:02:22,025
Low-stock and out-of-stock notifications are created automatically.

34
00:02:23,025 --> 00:02:27,684
The Sales page lets the admin search transactions, view receipts,

35
00:02:27,684 --> 00:02:30,050
export to CSV, and refund orders.

36
00:02:31,050 --> 00:02:34,751
In Products, each menu item has a recipe per serving.

37
00:02:34,751 --> 00:02:37,475
This links every sale to the inventory.

38
00:02:39,800 --> 00:02:43,638
Raw materials are tracked in grams, milliliters, or pieces,

39
00:02:43,638 --> 00:02:45,850
each with its own low-stock level.

40
00:02:46,850 --> 00:02:51,653
When a delivery arrives, the admin records the quantity and purchase cost.

41
00:02:51,653 --> 00:02:53,600
Here, five liters of oat milk.

42
00:02:54,800 --> 00:02:57,710
Stock updates immediately, the alert clears,

43
00:02:57,710 --> 00:03:00,950
and a weighted-average cost values the inventory.

44
00:03:01,950 --> 00:03:06,226
Cash Management shows every cashier shift, with the expected cash,

45
00:03:06,226 --> 00:03:07,975
counted cash, and variance.

46
00:03:08,975 --> 00:03:13,825
Reports show daily revenue, top-selling products, and the payment method mix.

47
00:03:15,025 --> 00:03:20,564
The inventory report covers stock value, deliveries, ingredient usage,

48
00:03:20,564 --> 00:03:21,435
and alerts.

49
00:03:21,435 --> 00:03:24,125
Both reports export to PDF or CSV.

50
00:03:25,125 --> 00:03:29,106
In Settings, the admin manages their profile and password,

51
00:03:29,106 --> 00:03:33,225
and uploads the G-Cash and Maya QR codes used by the tablet.

52
00:03:34,225 --> 00:03:39,380
In summary: Cash, G-Cash and Maya payments, automatic recipe-based inventory,

53
00:03:39,380 --> 00:03:43,330
low-stock alerts, shift reconciliation, exportable reports,

54
00:03:43,330 --> 00:03:45,406
and Bluetooth receipt printing.

55
00:03:45,406 --> 00:03:46,075
Thank you!
